A||N||14||87ECO5||3.4 Fiero wouldn't start yesterday morning but did this afternoon||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||10-18-2001||09:23 PM||||Wasn't sure what to put in the subject header.  Hope it draws some attention.  Here's the abbreviated story:<P>Yesterday morning, I went to start my car.  Turned the key on but the fuel pump didn't pressurize and the car wouldn't start.  This afternoon, without doing anything (except wait for warmer weather), the fuel pump pressurized and the car started on the first attempt.<P>Any ideas?<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||10-18-2001||09:39 PM||||May be a sticking fuel pump relay?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||LivoniaFieroGT||10-18-2001||09:55 PM||||Well before real midwestern cold weather comes ya better get it fixed or it'll be getting pushed into storage.  I agree... check the relay.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||10-18-2001||10:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LivoniaFieroGT:<BR><B>... or it'll be getting pushed into storage.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's where it is now.  I only drive it on occasion.  Last time I drove it was on 9/29.  Could sitting for almost three weeks be part of the problem?<P>I bought a new fuel pump relay this afternoon but didn't swap it in.  I'll do it this weekend.<P>Thanks, folks!||||reg||6
Z||000004||mrfiero||10-18-2001||10:44 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B> Could sitting for almost three weeks be part of the problem?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Doubtful.  My 16K mile '88 GT sits for months sometimes without being started.....when I do go to start it it fires right up.<P>I had another '88 GT that I didn't drive/start for almost a year (when I was in the Navy) and it started up just fine too.<P>Replace the relay and see what happens.  Have you ever replacedthe fuel pump?  That could be the problem too.<P>Good luck.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||10-18-2001||10:50 PM||||Scott, it's probably the relay. I think Ed changed the fuel pump when he made the engine swap. Or, check and make sure the fuse is good (it is the second from the left on the top row of the fuse box, a 5 amp fuse). I had one here recently where the fuse wasn't making good contact and the pump was intermittent.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87ECO5||10-19-2001||06:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>Have you ever replacedthe fuel pump?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, like Terry stated, Ed Parks swapped in a V6 pump when he converted my 4-cylinder car to the 3.4 engine.  However, since I went with the "used parts" option (cheaper), I don't know how many miles the fuel pump donor car had on it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||10-19-2001||08:08 AM||||I had a similiar problem and it turned out to be a loose battery connection.  At least that was all I adjusted.  Took the cable off and put it back on and the intermittant starting problem vanished.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||10-19-2001||12:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B> Yes, like Terry stated, Ed Parks swapped in a V6 pump when he converted my 4-cylinder car to the 3.4 engine.  However, since I went with the "used parts" option (cheaper), I don't know how many miles the fuel pump donor car had on it.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I would look into getting a new fuel pump.....it's cheap and easy to replace.  I only recommend using an AC Delco pump though......I just had to replace the fuel pump on my daily driver '88 GT even though the previous owner had it replaced a year ago.  It was an aftermarket pump and pooped out in a year.<P>I think it's at least a peace of mind thing.....knowing you have a new, proper fuel pump is comforting when problems arise (at least you can then rule it out as a factor).<P>Did replacing the relay do anything? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||87ECO5||10-25-2001||09:18 AM||||Guess what?  It happened again today.  Went up at 7:00 to get her, only this time I heard the pump pressurize but the car STILL didn't start.  Screamed a few vulgarities then took my daughter to school.  After dropping her off, I decided to try again.  It's now 8:30.  I get in and turn the key.  The car starts immediately!  HOWEVER ...<P>The belt is squealing like a stuck pig!  There's a huge puddle of oil underneath the car.  I drive out of the storage place where I keep it, the car cuts out two or three times, I hear a soft pop, and the "SES" light comes on.  By the time I get to work, the idle is bouncing ... are you ready for this? ... 1000 RPMs!!!!!  From 2100 to 1100 and back!<P>WTF!?!?!?!?!?!?!?||||reg||8
Z||000010||redfiero||10-25-2001||11:15 AM||||Scott,<P>Did you talk to Ed about it yet?<P>matt||||reg||1
Z||000011||87ECO5||10-25-2001||01:09 PM||||Hey, Matt!!!  How've you been?<P>No, I haven't spoken with Ed yet.<P>BTW, pulled the code over lunch.  In addition to the 32 (EGR) and 35 (IAC???) that have been there for a few months, the latest is a 21 (TPS).||||reg||6
